curve within the reviewed scores; when it stays below \code{target}, no score
guarantees the target (\code{reaches_target = FALSE}).
\item \code{threshold_precision}: the lowest score from which the precision of the
clips kept, as predicted by the curve (the mean of the predicted
probabilities of the reviewed clips at or above the cut, weighted by
\code{1 / inclusion_prob}), stays at or above \code{target}. It answers the same
question as the weighted count, \code{threshold_weighted}, so
\code{diff_weighted} (their difference) is direct evidence on the shape of
the curve.
