\strong{Verdict.} One per group, following the decision table of the
threshold workflow:
\itemize{
\item \code{"too_few_clips"}: fewer than \code{min_n} clips, or fewer than two of
either verdict; no curve is fitted.
\item \code{"sample_more_near_threshold"}: fewer than \code{min_n} effective clips in
the high score bins; a new round there (\code{sampling_mode = "score_bands"} in \code{\link[=select_clips]{select_clips()}}, joined by \code{\link[=combine_rounds]{combine_rounds()}}) is
needed before deciding.
\item \code{"no_curve_reaches_target"}: neither the flexible curves nor the
weighted count give a threshold with precision \code{target} (with at least
\code{min_n} effective clips above it). The curve levels off before the
target, or reaches it only at the very top, and no usable score
guarantees it: improve the classifier before setting a threshold.
